@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: PROPOSED — what a credential field must guarantee, and the screen that proves the secret is spendable
' PROPOSAL, not shipped behaviour. Sibling of init-credential-wireframe.puml, which owns screen 1.
'   the plan ................... _spec/_plans/init-credential-provisioning.puml
'   what the agent may hold .... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'
' ── SUPERSEDED: THE FIELD MOVED INTO THE LIST ──────────────────────────────
' Screen 2 was a separate hidden prompt, read after the form exited. The
' operator's direction of 2026-09-16 put the input in the list itself, one
' masked field per credential, so init-credential-wireframe.puml now owns the
' typing and this file keeps the rules that field must obey and the screen that
' follows it. Both drawings are kept: the rules did not change with the shape.
'
' WHAT THE FIELD MUST STILL GUARANTEE, wherever it is drawn: masked while
' typing, never echoed, never an argv word, never written to a file proveo owns,
' and handed to `sbx secret set` on stdin. A tcell form holds a redraw buffer,
' so the value lives there for the length of the form and nowhere else — it is
' zeroed on accept and on cancel alike.
'
' Enter on an empty field leaves that credential as it was. The answer to "I
' typed in the wrong row" is to clear it, not esc, which discards every answer
' given so far.
'
' ── SCREEN 3 ANSWERS "SPENDABLE", NOT "PRESENT" ────────────────────────────
' The suite already measures a credential that exists and is refused: a valid
' ANTHROPIC_API_KEY with an empty wallet returns 200 to a models request and
' 401 to a message. So VERIFY is one authenticated request against a cheap
' endpoint, and its three outcomes are drawn distinctly:
'   accepted ..... the provider answered 2xx
'   refused ...... the provider answered — and said no. The store keeps the
'                  value; hiding it would make the next run's 401 a mystery.
'   unverified ... proveo knows no cheap authenticated endpoint for this
'                  provider (cursor has none published). Never drawn as good,
'                  never drawn as bad.
'
' ── THE STORE IS WRITTEN UNDER TWO NAMES, AND THE SCREEN SAYS SO ───────────
' The broker path reads the SERVICE id; the forward path and every harness read
' the ENV VAR name. Until that map lands, one secret occupies two entries, and
' an operator reading `sbx secret ls` would otherwise find a duplicate they did
' not create and delete one at random.

title PROPOSED · the field's rules, and the screen that proves the value is spendable

{
{+
  ==screen 2 · the field, now an item in the list — masked as it is typed
  {
    . | <color:#9a9a9a>drawn in full in init-credential-wireframe.puml; the rules are this file's
    anthropic | "••••••••••••••••••••         "
    . | <color:#9a9a9a>masked · not in argv · not written to any file proveo owns
    . | <color:#9a9a9a>Enter on an empty field leaves anthropic as it was
    opencode | "                             "
  }
  ~~
  ==screen 3 · what was written, and whether it is spendable
  {
    <color:#00BAC6><&check></color> | anthropic | stored as | anthropic <b>and</b> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
    . | . | verified | <color:#00BAC6>the provider accepted it</color>
    <color:#00BAC6><&check></color> | opencode | stored as | opencode <b>and</b> OPENCODE_API_KEY
    . | . | verified | <color:#E8A33D>stored, but the provider answered HTTP 401 — present is not spendable</color>
    <color:#9a9a9a><&circle-check></color> | cursor | stored as | cursor <b>and</b> CURSOR_API_KEY
    . | . | verified | <color:#9a9a9a>no cheap authenticated endpoint — not verified either way</color>
  }
  --
  the env vars keep working; the store now outranks them, and a run says which one it spent
}
{
{^"A · refused is reported, never swallowed"
  <color:#E8A33D><&warning></color> | opencode | HTTP 401
  .
  The value stays in the store. Deleting
  it on a 401 is how an operator retypes
  a good key three times against an empty
  wallet — the failure this reports is the
  provider's answer, not the typing.
}
{^"B · a login is the agent's, and needs no field"
  claudecode | <color:#9a9a9a>nothing to type
  .
  /login belongs to the agent. Run it,
  and the def's declared home set —
  .claude and .claude.json — carries it
  out at teardown and back at seed, so
  proveo never sees the token.
  .
  Screen 2 offers a field only for a
  credential the operator holds as a
  STRING: an api key, or a token minted
  on the host with `claude setup-token`.
}
{^"C · nothing chosen — no screen 2"
  . | <color:#9a9a9a>every row left as is
  .
  The stage ends at the report. An init
  that asks for nothing when nothing was
  chosen is what makes it safe to run
  again on a host that is already set up.
}
}
}
@endsalt
